# rules.llm — Repository guardrails for coding agents & contributors

This file is **policy** and is intentionally version-controlled. The
reference/spec/export documents it protects are **not**.

## Never commit, stage or push

| Class | Examples / patterns |
|---|---|
| Postman exports | `*.postman_collection.json`, `*.postman_environment.json`, anything under `postman/` |
| API & auth specs | `ALL_APIs.md`, `AUTHENTICATION_LOGIN_FLOW.md` |
| Reference guides | `*_GUIDE.md` (e.g. `FRONTEND_*_GUIDE.md`) |
| Planning docs | `*_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` |
| Secret material | `*.pem`, `*.key`, `*.p12`, `*.pfx`, `*.keystore`, `*.jks`, real `.env` files |
| Test evidence | one-off tokens, captured HTTP dumps, screenshots of secrets |

These routinely contain live access tokens, refresh tokens, invitation
tokens, passwords and internal endpoint maps. They belong in the team wiki /
secret manager / ticket, **never** in Git.

## Required checks before every commit

```sh
git status --short                 # confirm nothing unexpected is staged
git diff --cached --name-only      # eyeball the exact file list
```

If any protected file is staged, unstage it (`git restore --staged <path>`)
and add it to `.gitignore` if it is missing.

A tracked hook (`.githooks/pre-commit`) enforces the list above. Enable it
once per clone:

```sh
git config core.hooksPath .githooks
```

## What *is* allowed

- Application source and tests (`src/**`, `*.test.tsx`, …).
- Repo policy/config files: `README.md`, `rules.md`, `rules.llm`,
  `package.json`, `tsconfig*.json`, `.env.example` (template only, **no real
  values**), CI/workflow files.
- Short-lived operational notes only when they contain no credentials or
  internal topology.

## If a protected file was already pushed

Deleting it in a later commit is **not** enough — it stays in history. Purge
it with `git filter-repo` (see the repo's security runbook) and rotate any
credential it exposed. Assume every token that was ever pushed is compromised.
